People nowadays are talking about whether the most essential aim of science is to improve our lives or not. Some disagree, but I firmly believe that it is true. This essay will demonstrate this through personal effects and effect for the society.

The primary reason is that science improves people's lives personally. This is because new medicine helps people become healthier. Consequently, they can enjoy a better quality of life. For instance, vaccines protect people from dangerous diseases. This shows that science directly benefits individuals.

Another important consideration is that science helps society develops. If scientists continue making new discoveries, the country will become more advanced. In other words, scientific progress makes society way stronger. A case in point is the Internet, which has improved communication and business around the world. Therefore, science also creates benefits for society.

Admittedly, people might contend that animals should be involved too. But they overlook that animals has the ability to be independent and do not need to aim for that. 

In conclusion, despite concerns about animals, I maintain that the most essential aim of science is to improve our lives.